{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"161a487b434c811d","type":"text","text":"The hand-rubbing payoff for later:\n\nBecause that's how Grant operates: He notices things without immediately commenting on them.\n\n----\n\nThen, later, Emma starts rubbing her hands again.\n\nGrant just says something like, \"You can phase if you need to.\"\n\nEmma looks over. \"What?\"\n\n\"You always rub your hands first.\"\n\n----\n\nThat's a fantastic payoff. It rewards attentive readers exactly the same way it rewards Emma. It also tells Emma something she probably hasn't realized: Someone has been paying attention to her.","x":-200,"y":-200,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"88cdaaaa574ecaa8","type":"text","text":"Love also means letting someone carry you.","x":360,"y":-200,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"d083f791732f0885","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/other/Mindset.md","x":80,"y":-1040,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"fe6be301e65d45cf","type":"text","text":"The strongest part isn't \"wow, they're rich.\"\n\nThe strongest part is that Grant discovers what financial security actually feels like.","x":1520,"y":-80,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"69bcab7a0da7df8d","type":"text","text":"\"He's mentally losing that last sliver of the needing to hold himself together for Ben thing.\"\n\nInstead of:\n\n\"I have to hold myself together so Ben will be okay.\"\n\nIt slowly becomes:\n\n\"Ben is okay.\"","x":1520,"y":-720,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"55650d4c407ac696","type":"text","text":"Maybe at first Sara is trying to burn off the hurt of Savanna being gone sparring with Don, and it's not working, but comes to this realization, either from herself or Don, that while every chance she never got with Savanna is now so permanently gone, her boys need them. She can't be there for her daughter, but Sara can be there for these two young boys. It gives her something to do. She can move, she's not paralyzed by the loss. And that helps her stabilize. I would say she's kinda done this before, with the challenges she's faced before, someone in her family needed her. I mean, she's the woman that was turned without knowing about vampires, looked down at her pregnant belly, and accepted drinking blood because it was what her unborn child needed. ","x":760,"y":-680,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"a5ba0f69920dd7c4","type":"text","text":"Grant couldn't believe the numbers they were talking about. \n\nSome quiet part of him whispered that he didn't know that stupid job. \n\nWas it really that simple? \"You'll just give me that money\"\n\nOh maybe Anne talks about setting up a debit account for him, saying she'll need a little time to get a card with his name from the bank, and says to just use this one with her name on it in the mean time. ","x":2880,"y":-880,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"6f4d3d0bd496a2ce","type":"text","text":"Jane figured out how to make serious money selling her paintings back when I was a kid. Kaylie crafts jewelry that Anne markets are high class luxury items; non-family has to earn an invite to one of their exclusive parties just to view the merchandise.\"\n\n\"And you work for Death.\" Grant's voice was flat. \"Is Sara still in the military then?\"\n\n\"Only because I choose to, and no. Sara and Don aren't working, they're taking care of Cass. None of us have to work.\" Actually Emma hadn't worked most of her adult life. But after she'd gotten used to have a job and Brenda had left, she couldn't take being idle. \n\n\"I don't know.\" Grant's stomach was in knots, \"I just- I can't accept that kind of money. It's too much. I can't make that kind of money.\" If Sara had earned that money in the military then I was hers, not Grant's. \n\nEmma doubted that pointing out that none of them could when they were his age would land for him. So instead of his future, she turned to his past. \"You don't expect anything in return from Ben for all the money you've spent on him, right?\"\n\n\"Of course not.\" Grant's tone was sharp. \n\n\"Because he's family? That's how Sara feels about you.\" ","x":3520,"y":200,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"c701d2a6f57fe297","type":"text","text":"\"It's not a loan Grant. And none of us could earn that money at your age. Sara and Jane were barely making ends me when Me and Savanna was born. I know I don't look it, but don't forget that I'm the same age as Savanna. Sara was been a professional athlete and a bartender before she even started her military career. And she's spent plenty of time without an income, like right now.\" Emma sighed, \"I know this is an adjustment for you, but in this family we don't work because we have to. The same goes for you, Sara would rather see you not have a job than have one you hate. She won't say it out loud of course. My hot-headed red-haired mother is the opposite of warm and fluffy, but her expectations don't include a job unless it makes you happy.\"","x":3200,"y":-320,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"34b836bb12780f1f","type":"text","text":"I also pictured at some point Don calls Grant quirky or something like that, and Sara's like \"eh, we all are.\" And Don's like even me. And Sara's like \"see, that's your quirk, you don't have one\" And Don't like how does not being weird make me weird.\" And Sara's like \"you spend time with us.\"","x":760,"y":1360,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"e4d18d1c66e2644e","type":"text","text":"But when it comes to things like his sleep, there's inconsistency. \n\nSome nights he sleeps twelve hours.\n\nSome nights he barely sleeps.\n\nSome afternoons he's almost himself.\n\nOther afternoons he just... stares at the trees.\n\nRecovery isn't linear.","x":2040,"y":-1680,"width":400,"height":400}
	],
	"edges":[]
}